<title>CANADA: PanCanadian plans C$1.1 bln oil project.</title>
<headline>PanCanadian plans C$1.1 bln oil project.</headline>
<dateline>WEYBURN, Saskatchewan 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>PanCanadian Petroleum Ltd said on Thursday it will spend C$1.1 billion to extend production at an oilfield in southeast Saskatchewan.</p>
<p>&quot;It gives me great pleasure to announce the C$1.1 billion plan to extend the Weyburn oil project for another 25 years using carbon dioxide to extract an additional 122 million barrels,&quot; PanCanadian Chief Executive officer David Tuer told reporters on a conference call.</p>
<p>The company is Canada's second largest oil firm.</p>
</text>
